<title>UK: South Africa Oct sugar output rises year/year - ISO.</title>
<headline>South Africa Oct sugar output rises year/year - ISO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa produced 313,425 tonnes of sugar in October, up on the 224,417 tonnes turned out in the same month in 1995, the International Sugar Organization (ISO) said on Tuesday. Cumulative sugar production for the first 10 months of this year amounted to 1.93 million tonnes, compared with 1.36 million for the same period in 1995, the ISO said.</p>
<p>The South African campaign runs from May to December.</p>
<p>October sugar exports were sharply higher this year at 175,223 tonnes after a previous 75,004 tonnes, bringing the total January/October export figure to 737,759 tonnes.</p>
<p>Sugar exports reached 353,746 tonnes for the first 10 months of 1995, the ISO said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
